      <body>
          <div type="edition" xml:lang="kan-Latn" rendition="class:kannada maturity:middle">
              <p>
                  <lb n="1"/>svasti śrī-cāḷu<choice><orig>khya</orig><reg>kya</reg></choice>-permānaḍi-<choice><orig>prithuvi</orig><reg>pr̥thvī</reg></choice>
                  <lb n="2"/>-rājyaṁ geyyutt’ ire <choice><orig>sakha</orig><reg>śaka</reg></choice>-kālaṁ <choice><sic>noṁbhai</sic><corr>oṁbai</corr></choice>-nū
                  <lb n="3" break="no"/>ṟa-padināṟaneya vijaya saṁvatsara
                  <lb n="4" break="no"/>muṁ caitra-māsam āge</p> 
                  
              <p>kiṟuvusūra
                  <lb n="5" break="no"/>perggaliyara bijayita-gāvuṇḍana
                  <lb n="6"/>magaṁ Ammaḍi-gāvuṇdaṁ noḻaṁ
                  <lb n="7" break="no"/>beya gvārmmaṇḍana bhāgada dassiva
                  <lb n="8"/>bhāgaṁ goṇḍu keṟeya
                  <lb n="9"/>kaṭṭisidaṁ</p> 
                  
               <p>Idaṟa bittuvaṭṭava
                  <lb n="10" break="no"/>n aḻipu koṇḍava dēgulavaṁ basa
                  <lb n="11" break="no"/>diyumuṁ kavilyeyumaṁ keṟeyu
                  <lb n="12" break="no"/>maṁ bāṇarāsiyuman aḻidaṁ 
              </p>
              
              <p>
                  <lb n="13"/>I nālvaruṁ bittar·
              </p>
         </div>
          
        <div type="apparatus">
            
            <listApp>
                <app loc="8">
                    <lem source="bib:Krishna1935_01">bhāgaṁ goṇḍu keṟeya</lem>
                    <note>The editor of the inscription labels this line 7b as it seems to be inserted between the previous line and the next one.</note>
                </app>
            </listApp>

        </div>
         
          
          
          
        <div type="translation" source="bib:Krishna1935_01">
            <p n="1-4">Be it well. When the illustrious Cālukya-permmāḍi was ruling the earth, during the 916th year of the time of Śaka, the month of Caitra of the year Vijaya,</p>
            <p n="4-9"> Ammaḍi-gāvuṇḍa, son of Bijayita-gāvunda, <foreign>Pergaliyar</foreign> <foreign>(pergaḍe?)</foreign> of Kiṟuvusūr took the share  corresponding to one tenth(?) <foreign>(dassiva)</foreign> from the share of Noḷambeya-gvārmmaṇḍa and built the tank.</p>
            <p n="9-12">He who takes away the <foreign>bittavaṭṭa</foreign> of this will have destroyed the temple, <foreign>basadi</foreign>, tank and Bāṇarāsi (Benares).</p> 
            <p n="13">These four persons have made the gift.</p>
          </div>
        
